# Prettier is scoped to **/*.astro by the check/format scripts; Biome owns
# .ts/.tsx/.js/.mjs/.css/.json. These entries mirror biome.json's ignore set so the
# two tools can never disagree about a file, and so neither walks the gitignored
# Phase 0 playground (the D-02 scope fence).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SPLIT IS ENFORCED HERE, NOT ONLY DESCRIBED ABOVE.
#
# The header said Prettier "is scoped to **/*.astro by the check/format scripts",
# and that was true of the scripts and false of the tool: `prettier --write
# "test/**/*.ts"` typed by hand reformatted about twenty test files into Prettier's
# style, which Biome then reported as twenty format errors. The mistake was caught
# by `npm run check` and cost a detour to undo.
#
# Ignoring the extensions Biome owns makes the same command a no-op instead. The
# scripts still pass `**/*.astro` explicitly, so nothing about the intended path
# changes; only the unintended one stops working.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.ts
*.tsx
*.js
*.mjs
*.cjs
*.css
*.json
*.jsonc

node_modules/
dist/
.astro/
.wrangler/
.playground/

# generated — regenerated by `wrangler types` in the dev/build/preview scripts
worker-configuration.d.ts
package-lock.json

# not this project's source: data/ is the git-as-database content (Phase 3 owns its
# formatting), design_handoff_portfolio/ is exported design-tool output, public/ ships
# verbatim, .planning/ is prose.
data/
design_handoff_portfolio/
public/
.planning/
